            "content": "### Planning and Designing of Audit: Entity Profiling, Risk Analysis & ADM\n\n1. **Understanding the Auditee Entity**:\n   - Legislative mandate, organizational structure, fund flows, schemes, accounting systems, and internal controls.\n2. **Desk Review**:\n   - Scrutiny of prior year Inspection Reports, CAG Audit Reports, budget documents, Appropriation Accounts, Finance Accounts, utilization certificates, and media reports.\n3. **Risk Analysis & Risk Assessment Parameters**:\n   - Identifying areas of inherent risk, control risk, and high financial materiality.\n   - Risk profiling to prioritize units and expenditure heads for field inspection.\n4. **Audit Design Matrix (ADM)**:\n   - A structured tabular framework formulated before commencing field audit:\n     - *Column 1: Audit Question / Objective* (What is being evaluated?)\n     - *Column 2: Sub-Questions* (Specific facets of the objective)\n     - *Column 3: Audit Criteria* (Rules, norms, standards, scheme guidelines)\n     - *Column 4: Required Evidence* (Vouchers, registers, digital logs, contracts)\n     - *Column 5: Methodology / Data Collection* (Sampling, interview, data analytics, survey)\n     - *Column 6: Analysis Plan & Expected Findings*",
