            "content": "### Audit Execution: Field Procedures & Evidence Protocols\n\n1. **Entry Conference**:\n   - Formal introductory meeting with executive leadership to communicate audit objectives, criteria, timelines, and logistics.\n2. **Audit Requisitions & Audit Enquiries**:\n   - Written requisition of files, registers, digital accounts, and contracts.\n   - Audit Enquiries (Half-Margins) issued when irregularities or non-compliance are identified.\n3. **Audit Evidence Characteristics**:\n   - Must be **Sufficient** (enough to convince a reasonable person).\n   - Must be **Competent** (reliable, authentic, third-party corroborated).\n   - Must be **Relevant** (logically connected to the audit criteria and finding).\n4. **Evidence Gathering Techniques**:\n   - Physical inspection, observation, re-calculation, confirmation, analytical review, and CAAT-based data queries.\n5. **Exit Conference**:\n   - Formal concluding meeting to present preliminary audit findings, verify factual accuracy, and record auditee management's official responses.",
