            "content": "### Audit Reporting in IA&AD: Products, Summaries & Report Qualities\n\n1. **Hierarchy of Audit Products**:\n   - *Audit Inspection Report (AIR)*: Issued to head of office containing Part I (Introduction), Part IIA (Major findings), Part IIB (Minor irregularities), Part III (Test check details).\n   - *Draft Paragraph (DP)*: Processed for inclusion in CAG Audit Report; sent to Administrative Ministry for response within 6 weeks.\n   - *Statement of Facts (SOF)*: Formal factual presentation sent to department.\n   - *Separate Audit Report (SAR)*: Formal audit certificate and comments on accounts of Autonomous Bodies and statutory corporations.\n   - *CAG Audit Reports (Civil, Commercial, Compliance, Performance, Financial)*: Tabled in Parliament / State Legislatures.\n2. **Executive Summary**:\n   - High-impact, jargon-free synthesis placed at the beginning of Performance Audit reports highlighting key findings, financial impact, and major recommendations.\n3. **Characteristics of a Good Audit Report**:\n   - *Accuracy & Objectivity*: Supported 100% by documented working papers.\n   - *Clarity & Conciseness*: Simple language avoiding bureaucratic ambiguity.\n   - *Tone*: Balanced, professional, avoiding sensationalism.\n   - *Constructive*: Providing systemic remedies rather than mere fault-finding.",
