            "content": "### Descriptive Statistics and Data Representation in Audit\n\n1. **Data Types in Public Accounts**: Nominal, Ordinal, Interval, and Ratio scale data (voucher numbers, risk grades, transaction amounts).\n2. **Frequency Distribution**: Grouping transaction data into class intervals to analyze expenditure patterns.\n3. **Graphical Tools for Audit Analysis**:\n   - *Histogram*: Distribution of voucher values and payment frequency.\n   - *Frequency Polygon*: Comparing expenditure trends across financial years.\n   - *Ogive (Cumulative Frequency Curve)*: Determining median expenditure and percentile cut-offs.\n   - *Pie Chart & Bar Chart*: Composition of revenue receipts and departmental outlays.",
