            "content": "### Computer Architecture: Hardware Components and Memory Hierarchy\n\n1. **Central Processing Unit (CPU)**:\n   - *Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU)*: Performs arithmetic operations (addition, subtraction) and logical comparisons (AND, OR, NOT).\n   - *Control Unit (CU)*: Decodes instructions, manages fetch-decode-execute cycle, and orchestrates data flow between CPU, memory, and I/O devices.\n   - *Registers*: High-speed internal memory cells (Program Counter, Instruction Register, Accumulator, Memory Address Register).\n2. **Memory Hierarchy**:\n   - *Registers*: Fastest, smallest capacity, inside CPU.\n   - *Cache Memory (L1, L2, L3)*: High-speed SRAM situated between CPU and RAM to store frequently accessed instructions and data.\n   - *Primary Memory (RAM & ROM)*: RAM (Volatile, dynamic/static, working memory); ROM (Non-volatile, contains BIOS/UEFI firmware for bootstrap loader).\n   - *Secondary Storage*: SSD (NVMe/SATA flash memory), HDD (magnetic storage), optical/magnetic backup tapes.\n3. **Audit Perspective**: Verifying IT asset acquisition, technical specifications, server configuration compliance, and capacity utilization.",
