            "content": "### Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning Fundamentals in Audit\n\n### pp. 1-7: Artiﬁcial Intelligence\n\nArtiﬁcial Intelligence Strategy Framework COMPTROLLER AND AUDITOR GENERAL OF INDIA Artiﬁcial Intelligence Strategy Framework Artiﬁcial Intelligence Strategy Framework Ar ﬁcial Intelligence Strategy Framework Supreme Audit Ins tu on of India Artiﬁcial Intelligence Strategy Framework Artiﬁcial Intelligence Strategy Framework Preface The landscape of public audi ng is undergoing a signiﬁcant transforma on driven by emerging technologies. In par cular, Ar ﬁcial Intelligence (AI) has surfaced as a powerful enabler in enhancing audit precision, eﬃciency, and scope. Recognizing the pivotal role that AI can play in advancing the objec ves of public accountability, transparency, and data-driven governance, this document outlines the Ar ﬁcial Intelligence Strategy Framework for the Indian Audit and Accounts Department. This Strategy Framework seeks to provide structured guidance on the adop on and integra on of AI tools and techniques across the audit lifecycle. The Government of India is increasingly using AI in various applica ons and pla orms, and thus it is per nent for us to have framework and capacity to audit such systems, which is in compliance with the responsible AI principles. This document deﬁnes the processes for undertaking such an exercise. It is designed to support audit oﬃcials in leveraging AI to augment tradi onal audit methodologies, enabling smarter data analysis, anomaly detec on, risk assessment, and predic ve insights. The framework also underscores key considera ons related to ethical use, data privacy, model governance, and capacity building. The document is intended to serve as a reference for ﬁeld audit teams, func onal group coordinators, and policy divisions alike, facilita ng a shared understanding of AI-enabled prac ces within the department. It also reﬂects the commitment of the Comptroller and Auditor General of India to con nuously modernize public audi ng processes and align them with global technological standards. It is expected that this Strategy Framework will act as a catalyst in embedding AI into the core of audit opera ons, empowering our oﬃcials to address the complexi es of modern governance and deliver impac ul audit outcomes. (K. Sanjay Murthy) Comptroller and Auditor General of India April 2025 Artiﬁcial Intelligence Strategy Framework I Artiﬁcial Intelligence Strategy Framework Foreword The public audit landscape is evolving rapidly, driven by the exponen al growth of data and technological advancements. Among these, Ar ﬁcial Intelligence (AI) stands out as a transforma ve force—one that has the poten al to redeﬁne how audits are planned, executed, and evaluated. The Indian Audit and Accounts Department, with its mandate of ensuring transparency and accountability in public ﬁnance, must harness these emerging capabili es to stay ahead of the curve. The Ar ﬁcial Intelligence Strategy Framework is a forward-looking ini a ve aimed at equipping audit professionals with the knowledge, tools, and strategies necessary to integrate AI into their day-to-day opera ons. This framework outlines a structured pathway for the adop on of AI applica ons in public audi ng, from anomaly detec on and predic ve analy cs to intelligent sampling and process automa on. In cra ing this strategy, care has been taken to ensure that the principles of audit integrity, ethical AI use, data security, and ins tu onal capacity building are deeply embedded. The framework also reﬂects our alignment with global best prac ces and our commitment to leveraging AI for high-impact, valueadded audits that respond to the complexity of modern governance. I am conﬁdent that this document will serve as a cornerstone in the Department’s journey towards digitally enabled and insight-driven audits. I encourage all oﬃcials to ac vely engage with the framework and become agents of transforma on in our shared pursuit of excellence in public audi ng. (S Ramann) Chief Technology Oﬃcer Oﬃce of the CAG of India April 2025 Artiﬁcial Intelligence Strategy Framework III\n\n---\n\n### pp. 8-14: Artiﬁcial Intelligence Strategy Framework\n\nArtiﬁcial Intelligence Strategy Framework Contents S. No. Chapter Name Page No. Chapter-1: Ar ﬁcial Intelligence 1.1. 1.2. 1.3. 4 Ar ﬁcial Intelligence - Concepts AI Ethics Ar ﬁcial Intelligence and Audit Chapter-2: Audit using AI 2.1. 2.2. 2.3. 2.3.1. 2.3.2. 2.3.3. 2.3.4. 2.4. 9 9 11 13 Adop ng AI in audit Broad Objec ves Scope of AI in Audit Audit Planning Audit execu on Audit Repor ng Audit Follow up Early applica on of AI in Audit – IA&AD use cases Chapter-3: Audi ng AI 3.1. 3.1.1. 3.1.2. 3.1.3. 3.2. 3.2.1. 3.2.2. 3.2.3. 3.2.4. 3.3. 3.3.1. 3.3.2. 3.3.3. 3.3.4. 17 18 19 20 22 22 23 Audi ng AI systems AI Regulatory framework AI Maturity level of the audited en ty Ecosystem for AI Audi ng Audi ng AI systems - Audit Objec ves Whether there are appropriate AI Governance mechanisms in the en ty? Whether the AI system has been developed appropriately? Whether the AI system delivers the intended output or not? Whether the AI system is safe and secure? Audi ng AI systems - Audit Process Audit Approach Audit Planning Audit Execu on Audit Repor ng and Follow up Artiﬁcial Intelligence Strategy Framework V Chapter-4: AI- The way forward 4.1. 4.2. 4.2.1. 4.2.2. 4.2.3. 29 30 Challenges of AI Implementa on Ar ﬁcial Intelligence – Implementa on Strategy Research and Applica on Training and Capacity Building Infrastructure and resource requirements Conclusion Annexure-1: Regulatory Frameworks Annexure-2: Illustra ve checklists VI Artiﬁcial Intelligence Strategy Framework 1 CHAPTER Ar ﬁcial Intelligence Artiﬁcial Intelligence Strategy Framework Artiﬁcial Intelligence Strategy Framework Chapter-1: Ar ﬁcial Intelligence Ar ﬁcial Intelligence is an advanced computer system that can simulate human capabili es, such as analysis, based on a predetermined set of rules.1 AI has made advancements in recent years, driven by sophis cated algorithms, increased computa o\n\n1. **Core AI/ML Paradigms**:\n   - *Artificial Intelligence (AI)*: Simulation of human intelligence processes by computer systems (reasoning, problem-solving, pattern recognition).\n   - *Machine Learning (ML)*: Subset of AI where algorithms learn patterns from training data without being explicitly programmed.\n   - *Supervised Learning*: Algorithms trained on labeled data (Regression, Classification - e.g. predicting fraudulent vs legitimate reimbursement claims).\n   - *Unsupervised Learning*: Discovering hidden patterns in unlabeled data (Clustering, K-Means - e.g. grouping vendor bidding patterns to detect cartels).\n   - *Natural Language Processing (NLP)*: Processing unstructured text (parsing contracts, extracting audit findings from court judgments, sentiment analysis).\n2. **Audit Applications in IA&AD**:\n   - Anomaly detection in high-volume treasury transactions.\n   - Automated contract clause extraction and compliance checking.\n   - Predictive risk-based audit planning and unit selection.",
