            "title": "CAAT Tools & SQL Data Analytics Practical: Knime, Tableau & Query Exercises",
            "content": "### Practical CAAT Tools and SQL Data Analytics for Auditors\n\n1. **Knime Analytics Platform Workflow**:\n   - *File Reader / Excel Reader*: Ingest raw transaction dumps.\n   - *Missing Value Node*: Handle NULL values in financial fields.\n   - *Row Filter / Rule-based Row Filter*: Filter payments above statutory thresholds.\n   - *Joiner Node*: Perform Left Outer Join between sanctioned works and contractor payments to find payments without sanctions.\n   - *GroupBy Node*: Aggregate total expenditure per vendor to spot contract monopolization.\n2. **Tableau Visual Analytics**:\n   - Connecting to database, building interactive worksheets.\n   - Heat maps showing expenditure spikes in March (March Rush phenomenon).\n   - Treemaps displaying departmental budget utilization percentages.\n3. **Practical SQL Audit Exercises**:\n   - *Detecting Split Sanctions*:\n     ```sql\n     SELECT DDO_Code, Sanction_Date, COUNT(*), SUM(Amount)\n     FROM Sanctions\n     WHERE Amount BETWEEN 450000 AND 499999\n     GROUP BY DDO_Code, Sanction_Date\n     HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;\n     ```\n   - *Detecting Weekend / Holiday Payments*:\n     ```sql\n     SELECT Voucher_No, Voucher_Date, Amount\n     FROM Vouchers\n     WHERE strftime('%w', Voucher_Date) IN ('0', '6');\n     ```",
            "gist": "Practical exercises use Knime for ETL and joins, Tableau for March rush visualization, and SQL queries to identify split sanctions, duplicate bills, and weekend payments.",
            "crux": "1. Split sanctions are identified by transactions clustering just below approval limits.\n2. Knime Joiner Node identifies unvouched expenditures or unlinked sanctions.\n3. Tableau heatmaps immediately flag end-of-financial-year March rushes.",
