            "title": "1. Fundamental Rules & Supplementary Rules (Part I): (d) Retirement",
            "content": "### Retirement Rules under Fundamental Rule 56\n\n1. **Superannuation Age (FR 56(a))**: Every government servant retires on the afternoon of the last day of the month in which he attains 60 years of age (if born on 1st of month, on last day of preceding month).\n2. **Premature Retirement in Public Interest (FR 56(j))**:\n   - Absolute right of Government to retire in public interest:\n     - Group A & B officers who entered service before age 35 upon attaining age 50.\n     - In all other cases, upon attaining age 55.\n   - Requires **3 months' notice** in writing or 3 months' pay and allowances in lieu of notice.\n3. **Voluntary Retirement (FR 56(k) / Rule 48)**: Government servant may seek voluntary retirement after attaining age 50/55 or completing 20/30 years of qualifying service by giving 3 months' notice.",
