            "title": "4. Central Civil Services (Joining Time) Rules",
            "content": "### CCS (Joining Time) Rules 1979\n\n1. **Applicability**: Granted to government servants on transfer in public interest to enable them to join new post at another station.\n2. **Entitlement Calculations**:\n   - Distance <= 1,000 km: **10 days**.\n   - Distance > 1,000 km and <= 2,000 km: **12 days**.\n   - Distance > 2,000 km: **15 days** (except by air travel where entitlement is 12 days).\n   - Transfer within same station or no change of residence: **1 day** (or nil if in same building).\n3. **Unavailed Joining Time**: Automatically credited to Earned Leave account, subject to maximum ceiling of 300 days.",
            "gist": "Joining time: 10 days (<=1000 km), 12 days (1001-2000 km), 15 days (>2000 km), and 1 day within same station. Unavailed joining time is credited to EL.",
            "crux": "1. Up to 1000 km = 10 days; 1001 to 2000 km = 12 days; >2000 km = 15 days.\n2. Unavailed joining time credited to EL account.\n3. Not admissible for temporary transfers up to 180 days.",
