            "content": "### Government Accounting Standards Advisory Board (GASAB)\n\n1. **Establishment**: Constituted in 2002 by the Comptroller and Auditor General of India with the support of the Ministry of Finance, Government of India.\n2. **Structure**: Chaired by Deputy CAG; members include representatives from Ministry of Finance (Budget Division, CGA, Controller General of Defence Accounts), State Finance Secretaries, RBI, and ICAI.\n3. **Core Responsibilities**:\n   - Formulating Indian Government Accounting Standards (IGAS) for the cash system of accounting.\n   - Formulating Indian Government Financial Reporting Standards (IGFRS) for the progressive transition to accrual accounting.\n   - Developing accounting templates for Natural Resource Accounting (NRA).",
            "gist": "GASAB was established in 2002 to formulate standards for government accounts (IGAS for cash accounting and IGFRS for accrual transition).",
