            "id": "pc11_s5_c2",
            "chapterNum": 2,
            "title": "(ii) Indian Government Accounting Standards (IGAS 1, 2 and 3) notified by Government of India",
            "content": "### Notified Indian Government Accounting Standards (IGAS 1, 2, 3)\n\n1. **IGAS 1: Guarantees Given by Governments: Disclosure Requirements**:\n   - Mandates comprehensive disclosure of all sovereign guarantees given by the Union and State Governments to public sector undertakings, local bodies, and financial institutions.\n   - *Disclosures*: Purpose, maximum amount guaranteed, outstanding amount, invocation of guarantees during year, guarantee fee received and in arrears (incorporated in Statement 9 of Finance Accounts).\n2. **IGAS 2: Accounting and Classification of Grants-in-Aid**:\n   - Governs classification of grants given by Union to States and by States to local bodies.\n   - *Key Rule*: Grants-in-aid must be classified as **Revenue Expenditure** in the accounts of the grantor government, even if the funds are utilized by the recipient grantee for creating capital assets.\n   - Prescribes detailed disclosures in Statement 2 and Statement 10 of Finance Accounts.\n3. **IGAS 3: Loans and Advances Made by Governments**:\n   - Governs accounting and disclosure of loans extended by Government.\n   - *Disclosures*: Summary of loans by categories, terms and conditions, interest rates, repayments in arrears, loans written off, and confirmation of balances (incorporated in Statement 7 of Finance Accounts).",
            "gist": "IGAS 1 mandates complete disclosure of guarantees (Statement 9). IGAS 2 classifies all Grants-in-Aid as revenue expenditure in grantor accounts. IGAS 3 standardizes loan disclosures (Statement 7).",
            "crux": "1. IGAS 1: Guarantees disclosure (Statement 9 of Finance Accounts).\n2. IGAS 2: Grants-in-aid must be booked as Revenue Expenditure by grantor.\n3. IGAS 3: Loans and advances terms, arrears, and write-offs (Statement 7).",
